# Deny by default.
#
# The build context needs exactly one file: entrypoint.sh — the only COPY in the
# Dockerfile (every other step is apt/npm and reads nothing from the tree).
# Nothing else enters the context, so nothing that lives beside the tracked files
# can ride along by accident: local state, private notes and repository metadata
# are all covered by the `*` below. Listing them as extra rules would be dead
# config — they are excluded, not re-excluded.
#
# When a new COPY is introduced, whitelist it here. Until then the build fails
# loudly ("failed to compute cache key: ... not found") rather than silently
# shipping a context you did not intend.
*
!entrypoint.sh
